          "explanation": "The correct option is B because the professor specifically explained that when you take a loan, the transaction does not end there; you need to repay the loan along with interest over the term of the loan. This is a core part of the financing decision. Option A is the \"one-and-done\" fallacy trap. Option C is incorrect because if Interest Rate (r) ↑, the cost of borrowing increases, impacting cash flows. Option D is not supported by the lecture.",
