          "explanation": "The correct answer is B. The lecture explicitly noted that bond prices are usually expressed as a percentage of face value. A price of 95% means 95% of the face value. Calculating 95% of ₹1,000 gives ₹950. Distractor A (₹95) would be correct if the face value were ₹100, but the standard face value in the Indian context discussed (and the example of Infosys shareholders holding shares of face value typically in the thousands) implies a larger base. Distractor C (₹1,000) would be the price if the bond were trading at par (100%). Distractor D (₹9,500) results from mistakenly multiplying 95 by 100 instead of taking 95% of the face value.",
