      "created_at": "2026-11-04 08:38:01",
      "transcript_text": "Now, let us come to our problem 3. It says, An Attractive Investment offers a total return of 12%, over the coming year. Your friend thinks, the total real return on this investor. Investment will be only 8%. And therefore, the question before you is, what does your friend believe the inflation rate will be over the next year? So, essentially, in this problem, you are given with nominal interest rate, you are given with real interest rate, and you have to find out the inflation. Let us try to solve this problem. We understand that nominal rate of return is given to us as 12%, and real rate of return is given to us as 8%. We have to find out the rate of inflation. So, let us try to find it out. We understand that 1 plus r real equals 1 plus r nominal divided by 1 plus i. So, this implies our i will be equal to 1 plus r nominal divided by 1 plus r real minus 1. So, this implies our i will be equal to 1.12 divided by 1.08 minus 1. This implies that our i will come out as 3.7%. However, in this particular problem, we could have also computed our approximate solution. How? You understand that your real rate of return is approximately equal to nominal rate of return plus i. In other words, we can say that our i is approximately equal to r nominal minus r real. So, this implies our i is approximately equal to r nominal, which is 12% minus 8%. In other words, our i approximately will be equal to 4%. So, ideally in these kind of problems, you are expected to provide the precise answer. But, in day to day life, you can compute your approximate answer in these kind of problems.",
