      "transcript_text": "Now, let us come to limit orders. In the case of a limit order, the immediate execution is not guaranteed. Your order may get executed immediately, your order may not get executed immediately. So, the execution of the order is conditional on the limit price. Execution is conditional on the limit price. So, when you place a limit order, you have to specify three things. You have to specify the ticker, that you want to buy yourself, the number of shares or quantity that you want to buy yourself, and additionally, you have to also specify something called as limit price. Similar to market orders, even limit orders can be classified into two types. A limit order can be in order to buy shares, in which case we will call it as limit by order or it can be an order to sell shares, in which case we will call it as a limit sell order. In the case of a limit by order, for example, you will tell your broker that you want to buy, for example, ten shares of enforces at a price not exceeding 1000 rupees per share. In other words, your limit price here is 1000 rupees, and this order will be executed only if you have any value, if you are able to get shares of enforces at a price of 1000 rupees or lesser. In other words, your limit by order will be executed at a price less than or equal to limit price. So, your limit by order, it may or may not get executed. If it gets executed, it will get executed at a price of the limit price. Less than or equal to limit price. Similarly, you can also place a limit sell order. For example, you could tell your stock broker that you want to sell five shares of enforces at a price not less than 1100 rupees. This order may or may be not get executed. This order will only get executed if you are getting a price of at least 1100 rupees for each share of enforces. So, therefore, this order will be executed at a price which is going to be greater than or equal to limit price. If a limit order cannot be executed immediately, it is recorded in the stock exchanges limit order book till the time it is executed.",
